ashantor@yahoo.de (Ashantor) writes:
> in exper.c I found some information about the amount of XP I get for
> killing a monster.
> There is a "base" formula tmp = 1 + m_lev * m_lev, followed by lots of
> positive modifiers (speed, AC, attacktype, damagetype etc.).
> 
> In my current game my character uses a stethoscope to verify this
> data. Mission failed. He is now standing in front of the castle and
> got a lot more XP from killing monsters than he should. Almost every
> killed foe was rewarded with more XP than expected. The only
> exceptions were monsters with m_lev = 0.

This is a bug, though it took me a little debug-pline adding to spot
it :-) The line "else if(tmp != AD_PHYS) tmp += mtmp->m_lev;" should
read "else if(tmp2 != AD_PHYS) tmp += mtmp->m_lev;"; as it stands,
it's awarding a spurious ML XP for every attack a monster _doesn't_
have, and for ones that only do physical damage (since tmp will always
be at least 1, which isn't AD_PHYS (0)). Cc'ed to the DevTeam.

